# Extended Hueckel parameters, one line per element and valence shell.
#
# WHY.  The extended Hueckel engine (FragmentOrbitals, also behind Huckel)
# needs orbitals for atoms from H to the 5d metals, with d shells.
#
# SOURCE.  S. Alvarez, "Tables of parameters for extended
# Hueckel calculations", Universitat de Barcelona, 1993, as distributed in
# eht_parms.dat of YAeHMOP (github.com/greglandrum/yaehmop, tightbind/).
# Copyright (C) 1995 Greg Landrum, BSD 2-clause licence (redistribution with
# the copyright notice, the licence conditions and the disclaimer, which
# are reproduced in docs/claude/mo-diagram/eht-parameters-and-licence.md).
# The values are copied unchanged; rows whose exponent is 0 in the source
# (placeholders: Ar, Kr, Xe, Y, Ag, Zn 3d, Cd 4d, and the p and d exponents of
# Hf, whose H_ii alone is given) are left out, so those elements have no
# parameters here.  No other published set could be read for them (see the
# docs entry); nothing in this file is derived or invented.  The source file gives no
# per-row references; the values were checked against Hoffmann's and
# Albright-Burdett-Whangbo's tables (see the docs entry).
#
# columns:  symbol  n  l  H_ii(eV)  zeta1  zeta2  c1  c2
# zeta in inverse bohr.  zeta2 = 0 means single zeta (c1 = 1).  The
# double-zeta d function is c1 STO(zeta1) + c2 STO(zeta2).
